{"sections":[{"estimatedTimeInMinutes":20,"image":"1-0-0.png","backgroundImage":"1-0-0.png","kind":"hero","title":"Delivering Reminders","chapter":"What's in a Reminder?","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Deliver Reminders to the user by formatting them and printing them to the terminal.","type":"text"}]}]},{"tasks":[{"contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a ReminderManager that keeps track of all active Reminders and prints them when necessary."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"anchor":"Building-a-ReminderManager","stepsSection":[{"type":"step","caption":[],"media":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Create a new ReminderManager.swift file.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"code":"2-1-1.swift","runtimePreview":null},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a variable stored property, "},{"code":"reminders","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReminderManager"},{"text":", so it can track the Reminders.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By setting this property to private, you can prevent other developers from making "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReminderManager"},{"type":"text","text":" remove a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Reminder"},{"type":"text","text":" when they shouldn’t."}]}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"2-1-2.swift","runtimePreview":null},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Create a function to add Reminders to your ","type":"text"},{"code":"reminders","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" collection."}]}],"code":"2-1-3.swift","caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because we don’t want others modifying our "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reminders"},{"text":" externally in whatever way they want, we’ll need to “wrap” one of the functions of that property with one of our own. This is a fairly common pattern when building containers on top of other containers, and is similar to (but not quite) the Decorator pattern.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","runtimePreview":null,"media":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To use the global sleep function, you need to import the library which defines it - Foundation."}]},{"media":null,"code":"2-1-4.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import Foundation and build a function called "},{"code":"run()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that will print our Reminders to the terminal after the duration has passed for that reminder."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because we are not yet building this async, our Reminders will print out sequentially, with each one’s duration ticking after the next.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"type":"step"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Currently this loses data due to casting from Double to UInt32 (it will floor any decimal values). This is OK for now, as future steps will fix this issue.","type":"text"}]}],"title":"Building a ReminderManager"},{"contentSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By using an instance of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReminderManager"},{"text":", we can keep track of our reminders and print them out as needed.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"title":"Building and Delivering Reminders In main.swift","anchor":"Building-and-Delivering-Reminders-In-mainswift","stepsSection":[{"media":null,"runtimePreview":null,"code":"2-2-1.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In main.swift, declare an instance of our ","type":"text"},{"code":"ReminderManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"caption":[],"type":"step"},{"code":"2-2-2.swift","type":"step","content":[{